# API Design Contract

## Versioning

- Business endpoints under `/api/v{N}` (initial: `/api/v1`).
- Platform endpoints unversioned: `/health`, `/ready`, `/metrics`. Mirrored under `/api/v1/health` and `/api/v1/ready` for clients pinned to v1.
- Breaking changes → new version (`/api/v2`); never break v1.

## Error envelope

```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Human-readable summary",
    "details": { "field": "reason" },
    "request_id": "uuid",
    "timestamp": "2026-04-27T19:00:00Z"
  }
}
```

- `code` is **stable** (clients depend on it). Use SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.
- Mapped centrally by `register_exception_handlers(app)`; do not hand-build envelopes in routes.

## Success shape

- Resource endpoints return the resource directly.
- List endpoints return:
  ```json
  { "items": [...], "page": { "number": 1, "size": 20, "total": 123 } }
  ```

## Headers (set by middleware)

- `X-Request-ID` — per-request correlation (accepted from client if valid, else generated).
- `X-API-Version` — `APP_VERSION`.
- `Content-Language` — resolved locale (BCP-47), echoed on every response that may contain user-visible text. See `i18n-l10n.mdc`.
- Security headers: `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`, `Strict-Transport-Security` (prod), `Content-Security-Policy` (strict on `/docs`).

## Locale negotiation (see `i18n-l10n.mdc` and spec §11)

- Clients send `Accept-Language: ar, en;q=0.9` and / or `?lang=ar`. Server resolves the locale (priority in `i18n-l10n.mdc`), echoes `Content-Language`.
- `error.message` is **translated** to the resolved locale; `error.code` is **always** locale-independent. Clients programmatic-match on `code`.
- Pagination labels and any other server-rendered text use the translator.
- Raw API dates/IDs stay locale-independent (ISO 8601 UTC). User-facing date/number/currency formatting uses Babel via `Translator.format_*`.

## Pagination

- `?page=1&page_size=20` with `page_size` ≤ **100** (enforced via `Depends(get_pagination)`).
- Cursor-based for high-cardinality lists — document per endpoint.

## Filtering / sorting

- `?filter[field]=value`, `?sort=field,-other`. Document allowed fields per endpoint.
- Reject unknown filter/sort keys (Pydantic on the dep).

## Idempotency

- Mutating endpoints accept `Idempotency-Key` header.
- Service hashes the `(endpoint, key)` pair; first response is cached in Redis for **24h**; later requests return the same response without re-running side effects.

## Content negotiation

- JSON only (`application/json`); `415 Unsupported Media Type` otherwise.
- Dates: RFC 3339 / ISO 8601, **always UTC** with `Z` suffix.
- Field naming: **snake_case** in JSON; URL paths **kebab-case**; collections plural lowercase nouns.

## HTTP status codes (use exactly these)

| Code | When |
|---|---|
| 200 | Read or RPC success with body |
| 201 | Created (set `Location`) |
| 202 | Accepted (queued async) |
| 204 | Success, no body |
| 400 | Malformed request (rare; Pydantic catches first) |
| 401 | Auth missing / invalid |
| 403 | Authenticated but not authorized |
| 404 | Not found |
| 409 | Conflict (duplicate / version mismatch) |
| 415 | Unsupported media type |
| 422 | Validation failed (Pydantic default) |
| 429 | Rate limited |
| 500 | Unexpected server error |
| 502 / 504 | Upstream failure / timeout |
| 503 | Not ready / draining |

## OpenAPI

- Every route has `summary`, `description`, `response_model`, **and** `responses={...}` for each documented error code.
- `/docs` and `/redoc` enabled in non-prod; gated or disabled in prod via `APP_DOCS_ENABLED`.
- `make openapi` exports `openapi.json` for CI consumers; PR shows a diff.
